#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Run a chosen main-run profile or selection on current origin/main by hand.

    tools/main-runs --now --tier fast
    tools/main-runs --now --tier ownership-trace
    tools/main-runs --now --select conformance/MODE/MODE-1-unique-local-taken-stays-local-bad.hir
    tools/main-runs --now --tier conformance --select conformance/MODE
    tools/main-runs --now --tier fast --select 'workspace tests' --dry-run

There is no automatic schedule. --now fetches origin/main, checks it out in
$HIRSEL_MAIN_RUNS/worktrees/main-runs and runs that copy. It reruns an unchanged
SHA when asked and refuses a concurrent run. --dry-run only lists the local
plan: it neither fetches nor consumes pool work. Stage selectors are name
prefixes within the chosen tier; corpus selectors are repository-relative
directories, cases or prefixes. Selections always prepare the pinned tools.

Fast retains the build, Clippy, fmt, workspace/tool tests, GenMC and fresh std
budget. The explicit conformance profile runs every interpreter directory in
at most 32 slices each; ownership-trace selects the registered diagnostic
runtime tests; native-smoke selects the existing conformance smoke list.
Full includes these profiles and the expensive release/native campaigns.
None is added to the land gate. Exception tables can skip named stages.

Reports in $HIRSEL_MAIN_RUNS/reports/ and latest.md list unrecorded failures
before known-owner counts per stage. An explicit green in the previous
completed run of that stage marks a failure NEW, with the full commit range
for a bisect. A first observation without a previous green stays unowned.
Wrongly accepted -bad cases appear first, including known failures. Existing
owner, code, infrastructure and exception-observation sections remain.
RUNNING.md publishes completed targets and command identities during a run;
only completed matching inputs can be reused. It is removed on completion.

The manual run also regenerates docs/api.md and can ratchet measured budgets;
these updates are pushed on main when changed. Invalid exception tables stop
execution. Reports and runs.jsonl retain exception_status v1 and execution
provenance. Only fresh complete exact passes are recovery candidates; cached,
partial, skipped and unobserved results are not recovery proof.
"""

